WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.875
Here's the subtle case the
chapter guards against.

2
00:00:02.875 --> 00:00:05.603
An intended state like
the one on the slide

3
00:00:05.603 --> 00:00:08.175
is a non-empty object,
so it looks present.

4
00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:12.075
But it names nothing: no
attribute, no entitlement.

5
00:00:12.075 --> 00:00:14.979
A re-read compares against
it, finds no difference,

6
00:00:14.979 --> 00:00:17.175
and would close the record on nothing.

7
00:00:17.175 --> 00:00:21.263
The check warns rather than rejects,
because ServiceNow would accept it.

8
00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:25.938
For the three classes the program sends
to a person first, missing identity,

9
00:00:25.938 --> 00:00:28.728
an orphan account and
an unauthorized write,

10
00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:32.500
the warning says that's expected
until that person decides.
